<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sunset Four Jubilee Singers (Paramount)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1925</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first commercial recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Revelations (Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">partly set to the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bob Dylan, Minnesota Hotel Tape</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ramsey Lewis Trio</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Herb Alpert and the Tijuana Brass; Billy Preston</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1967</span><span class="sg-chain-h">instrumental versions</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Chambers Brothers, Love, Peace and Happiness</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Little Walter (Tony! Toni! Toné!)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Eva Cassidy, Songbird</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wade in the Water, Children (documentary film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title taken from</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Migration: Reflections on Jacob Lawrence (&quot;The Wade Suite&quot;, Step Afrika!)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2011</span><span class="sg-chain-h">influenced by</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Savant, Overkill</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled in (Eva Cassidy's version)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Stand Up (from the film Harriet)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">referenced in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Book of Exodus (the Israelites' escape from Egypt)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the theme (2002 interpretation)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gospel of John 5:1–9 (the pool of Bethesda)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the troubled-water image (Howard Thurman and others)</span></li></ul></section>
